Fix the Apple II lo-res TGI driver: INSTALL has a stray 'bpl :+' (added with the
dynamic IIe check) whose target is the next anonymous label, inside HLINE. On a
non-enhanced Apple II it jumps into the middle of that code and the program
crashes in tgi_install(). INSTALL should just fall through to UNINSTALL.

--- a/libsrc/apple2/tgi/a2.lo.s
+++ b/libsrc/apple2/tgi/a2.lo.s
@@ -160,7 +160,6 @@
         ldy     #$0
         lda     (ptr1),y
         sta     machinetype
-        bpl     :+
         .endif
         ; Fall through
 
